Adapted classes: Node, Edge, GraphEltSet, Locality, VisibleLocality,
GESUtils, LocalityUtils, TGLayout, TGPanel, TGPoint2D, TGAbstractLens,
TGLensSet, and the HyperScroll lens calculations. The original code
notes that parts build upon Sun's Graph Layout example:
http://java.sun.com/applets/jdk/1.1/demo/GraphLayout/Graph.java

Reference: componavt/wikokit, commit
0db2310283d792abbaa57746fe9fe475fe9e6ab8
TGWikiBrowser/src/com/touchgraph/graphlayout/
https://github.com/componavt/wikokit/tree/0db2310283d792abbaa57746fe9fe475fe9e6ab8/TGWikiBrowser/src/com/touchgraph/graphlayout

The TypeScript adaptation replaces Java threads with event-loop scheduling,
Swing painting with SVG, and Java collections with JavaScript collections.
Core layout calculations follow TGLayout 1.21. The nonlinear lens follows
HyperScroll 1.06, including its sampled inverse. Locality additions at
equal distance use stable BFS ordering rather than Hashtable ordering.

Unmodified reference Java files used in tests retain their original
copyright and license headers. Headless test hosts and field carriers are
identified in their source comments and are not upstream implementations.

D3 dependencies (d3-selection, d3-drag, d3-zoom and their dependencies)
are distributed under their respective ISC licenses. See the installed
packages' LICENSE files. They supply browser interaction and rendering,
and do not replace the original spring layout engine.
